// synth-pad — a second use of the same "synth" module (see lead.k7x beside this file).
//
// Named for the lane it serves rather than after it: the lane "pad" is a node too now
// (nodes/pad.k7x), and one flat name space means one name, one node.
//
// Two nodes of one module are two separate chain steps with separate state: their
// params are merged independently over the module, and each saves its own opaque plugin
// blob (synth-pad.vstpreset here, lead.vstpreset next door), so tweaking one never touches
// the other or the module they share.
extends("@workspace/instruments/synth")
params({
  "Filter Freq": 40, // darker than the lead…
  Level: -12, // …and sitting further back
})
// Params merge per key, but a LIST is a scalar to the merge: restating `automations`
// replaces the inherited one outright. An empty list is how a node opts out of the
// filter sweep + detune LFO the module automates — the pad wants to sit still.
automations([])
